    healthcare: 'Several clinics and pharmacies inside the old city. Chiang Mai Ram Hospital is a short taxi/scooter ride away. For major healthcare needs, you go to the private hospitals outside the old city. Traditional Thai medicine and massage are extremely common — the Old City has hundreds of massage shops and traditional healing centers.',
    expatCommunity: 'The Old City has a large but transient expat community. Many expats pass through as tourists or short-term visitors. There is also a core of long-term residents — mostly retirees, yoga teachers, healers, artists, and people in the wellness/spiritual field. Americans who are interested in Buddhism, meditation, yoga, and Thai culture are drawn to the old city. The community is more spiritual and alternative than Nimman. There are lots of retreats, meditation courses, and yoga teacher trainings. It is not as party-focused or career-focused as other expat areas. The vibe is relaxed, gentle, and culturally rich.',
