      summary: 'Toumba is generally a safe neighborhood, especially considering its large student population. There is a lot of street life and people are out at all hours, which helps with safety. Petty crime (bike theft, phone theft, occasional break-ins) exists but is not out of control. The area has a lively, chaotic energy — lots of young people, bars, and activity. Some streets can feel a bit rough around the edges but are not dangerous. Normal university-neighborhood precautions apply: lock your bike, watch your belongings on busy nights, and be careful with your drink at bars. Most residents feel safe and enjoy the neighborhood\'s energy.'
