    lifestyle: ['Cultural / Historic', 'Peaceful / Quiet', 'Nature'],
    history: 'The Al Ain Oasis is the ancient heart of the city, inhabited for over 4,000 years. It is one of the largest oases in the UAE, with more than 147,000 date palm trees nourished by the ancient falaj ( aflaj ) irrigation system — a network of underground tunnels and surface channels that brings water from the nearby mountains. In 2011, the Al Ain Oasis was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site as part of the "Al Ain: Tawam and its Oases" site. The oasis includes the Al Ain National Museum, the Sultan Fort, and the historic Al Ain Palace Museum (former residence of Sheikh Zayed). The falaj system, still in use today, is considered one of the oldest and most sophisticated irrigation systems in the world.',
    safety: { score: 95, level: 'Very Safe', summary: 'Extremely safe — peaceful, low-traffic area with almost no crime.', tips: ['Very safe and peaceful area.', 'Follow the designated paths in the oasis — do not wander into private palm gardens.', 'The falaj water channels are deep — supervise children.', 'Wear comfortable walking shoes — it is a large area to explore.'] },
