    tags: ['Mountain', 'Nature', 'Adventure', 'Hot Springs', 'Scenic'],
    lifestyle: ['Outdoor / Adventure', 'Nature / Scenic', 'Peaceful / Quiet'],
    history: 'Jebel Hafeet is the highest peak in the Emirate of Abu Dhabi, rising 1,240 meters above the surrounding desert. The mountain marks the northern end of the Al Hajar mountain range that runs through the UAE and Oman. Its winding road, with 21 hairpin turns, was built in the 1970s and is considered one of the great driving roads in the world. At the base of the mountain are the Green Mubazzarah hot springs — natural warm springs that have been developed into a park with lakes, swimming pools, and picnic areas. The mountain is also famous for its caves, fossils, and diverse wildlife. Jebel Hafeet is the most popular weekend destination for Al Ain residents and tourists alike.',
