    history: 'Al Jahili is one of the oldest neighborhoods in Al Ain, centered around the historic Al Jahili Fort. The fort was built in the 1890s during the reign of Sheikh Zayed bin Khalifa Al Nahyan as a summer residence and strategic stronghold guarding the nearby oasis. The fort is renowned for its distinctive round towers and intricate crenellated mud-brick walls. In the 1950s, the famous British explorer Wilfred Thesiger (author of "Arabian Sands") was based in Al Jahili Fort during his expeditions across the Empty Quarter. Today the fort has been beautifully restored and houses a museum, exhibition halls, and a public garden. The surrounding neighborhood has preserved much of its traditional character, with palm groves, old mud-brick homes, and a quiet, historic atmosphere.',
