    lifestyle: ['Cultural / Historic', 'Peaceful / Quiet', 'Family-Friendly'],
    history: 'Al Muwaiji is a historic neighborhood in western Al Ain, centered around the Al Muwaiji Fort — a traditional 19th-century mud-brick fort with square and round towers. The fort is most famous as the birthplace of Sheikh Khalifa bin Zayed Al Nahyan, the late President of the UAE and Ruler of Abu Dhabi, who was born here in 1948. The fort has been beautifully restored and features an exhibition about the history of the Al Nahyan family and the development of Al Ain. Surrounding the fort are lush green gardens, date palm groves, and traditional Emirati architecture. The neighborhood has a quiet, dignified atmosphere reflecting its royal and cultural significance.',
